## The audit report to score (out-6)

~~~
# Pre-launch audit: Bäckerei Sonnenblume (site type: local-business)

**Scope.** I read the audit source and config as reference only and did not run the command. The site files are `index.html`, `impressum.html`, `kontakt.html`, `sortiment.html`, `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`.

**Region.** No region is declared in the supplied evidence, so the region is treated as `unspecified`. The base tiers apply and no DE escalation is applied.

**Skipped.** Nothing is skipped by the site-type rule. The checks that list only other site types, or that don't list `local-business`, would be skipped; none of those is needed here.

## Established defects

1. **Staging `noindex` left on the home page** (`staging-noindex-leftover`, critical)
   - File: `index.html`, line 7.
   - Defect: the home page tells search engines not to index it or follow its links.
   - Evidence: `<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />`.
   - The same URL (`https://baeckerei-sonnenblume.de/`) is listed in `sitemap.xml`, so the page is advertised and blocked at once.

2. **Blanket `Disallow: /` in robots.txt** (`staging-noindex-leftover`, critical)
   - File: `robots.txt`, line 2.
   - Defect: every crawler is barred from the whole site.
   - Evidence: `User-agent: *` followed by `Disallow: /`.
   - This is the second half of the staging-leftover defect the check names. It is separate from item 1 and needs its own fix.

3. **No custom 404 page** (`custom-error-route`, high)
   - Expected path: `404.html` (or a `not-found` page). It is absent site-wide.
   - Evidence: the tree holds only `index.html`, `impressum.html`, `kontakt.html` and `sortiment.html`, so none of the names the check looks for exists.
   - HTML pages are present, so the absence is decidable.

4. **Pages with no `<title>` and no meta description** (`per-route-metadata`, high)
   - Files: `kontakt.html` and `sortiment.html`.
   - Defect: each `<head>` contains only charset, viewport and canonical. There is no `<title>` and no `<meta name="description">`.
   - `index.html` and `impressum.html` do have both, so this is a per-route gap rather than a site-wide one.

5. **Content images without an `alt` attribute** (`image-alternative-text`, high)
   - `index.html`, line 12: `<img src="/laden.jpg" />`
   - `sortiment.html`, line 9: `<img src="/brot.jpg" />`
   - `sortiment.html`, line 10: `<img src="/kuchen.jpg" />`
   - None of these carries `alt`, not even `alt=""`, so a screen reader gets nothing.

6. **robots.txt contradicts the sitemap** (`canonical-and-sitemap-coherence`, medium)
   - Files: `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml`.
   - Defect: the sitemap advertises four URLs (`/`, `/sortiment`, `/kontakt`, `/impressum`), and `Disallow: /` blocks all of them. This is the "robots disallow on a route the sitemap advertises" case the check describes.
   - Canonical tags on all four pages do match their sitemap entries. The disagreement is only between robots.txt and the sitemap.
   - Fixing item 2 resolves this.

7. **No privacy / Datenschutz page** (`required-legal-pages`, situational at base tier)
   - Expected path: something matching `datenschutz` or `privacy`, such as `datenschutz.html` or `privacy.html`. It is absent site-wide.
   - Evidence: `impressum.html` exists, but no file path matches `datenschutz` or `privacy`.
   - This is reported at the base (situational) tier because no region is declared.

8. **Impressum is not linked from any page** (`required-legal-pages`, situational at base tier)
   - Files: `index.html`, `kontakt.html`, `sortiment.html` and `impressum.html`.
   - Defect: the check's title is "exist **and are linked**", and its remediation is to link the legal pages from the footer of every page. No page links to `/impressum`.
   - Evidence: the only anchor in the whole site is `<a href="/sortiment.html">` in `index.html`, and no page has a footer. The page exists but is unreachable by navigation (it is reachable only through the sitemap, which robots.txt blocks).
   - The supplied checker only matches legal pages by path. I am reporting this on the config's wording and its `verification` line (reachable from the home page in one click), not on a detector result.

## Passed or no defect found in the supplied files

- `https-enforcement`: no `http://` asset, link or form action appears in any page.
- `document-head-basics`: all four pages declare `lang`, charset and viewport.
- `analytics-and-consent-wiring`, `third-party-load-in-markup`, `privacy-page-provider-coverage`: no analytics tag or third-party load appears in the supplied files.
- `superseded-statute-in-legal-page` and `placeholder-in-legal-page`: `impressum.html` cites no TMG provision and has no bracketed placeholder.
- `snippet-eligibility` and `structured-data-parses`: there is no `nosnippet` or `max-snippet:0`, and no JSON-LD block.

## Uncertainties (not counted as defects)

- **Region.** The German language, the Freiburg address, the `.de` domain and the Impressum suggest a German audience, but no region is declared. I did not apply the DE escalation. Under `--region de`, items 7 and 8 would rise to critical in the config. Declare the region before treating the legal-page items as final.
- **Extensionless URLs.** The sitemap and canonicals use `/sortiment`, `/kontakt` and `/impressum`, while the only internal link is `/sortiment.html`. Whether the server rewrites these cannot be determined from the files, so I did not report it.
- **Deployment evidence.** The config's verifications for HTTPS redirects, `X-Robots-Tag` headers and real 404 responses need live HTTP data. None was supplied, so these are untested.
- **Unsupplied checker modules.** Modules such as `web_launch_head_checks` and the crawler register were not supplied. I judged items 1, 2 and 6 from the config's own definitions rather than from the checker's output.
- **Impressum content.** I did not assess whether the Impressum content is complete. That is a legal question outside this audit.
~~~

